  "notes": "muzi.co.il — Israeli live-music aggregator (WordPress, custom `event` post type, no REST route). Listing = /events-by-date/ (date-ascending, 10 real cards + 2 promo cards per page; /page/N/ via ?paged=N → 301 → followed): card = div.event.type-event with title/link (.avatar-name a), 'תחילת הופעה: HH:MM', venue+city text, price range; the DATE is NOT in the card (it sits in a sibling date header) and the venue text repeats the city, so both come from the detail hop instead: the event page's JSON-LD MusicEvent (startDate date-only, location.name, addressLocality, performer.name → artist_name) read via regex on the ld+json script text, plus the outbound seller link (kupat / tickchak / ticketmaster.co.il …) from the #popupWindowBox 'המשך בלי להרשם' anchor, which REPLACES the muzi page via detail.overwrite — purchase_link = the ticket seller, source_id = the muzi slug. Detail hop is only_new (250/run) so the first runs backfill ~1,000 upcoming events over a few days and steady state is ~80 listing + a few dozen detail requests. Rows the budget did not reach yet drop as no_date and are picked up next run; muzi still lists a handful of stale 2025 shows (dropped as past). raw_categories = the card's events_by_genre-* class. Not geo-walled from the Mac (Cloudflare-fronted; add relay if Render gets 403). Dry run 2026-09-20 (6 listing pages + 40 detail hops): 36 events, fill name/date/time/artist 100 %, venue+city 97 %, price 94 %; 18/36 already in prod (mevalim 15). Geo-walled: Render's fetch 403s /events-by-date/ (confirmed in /api/stats/recipes after the 2026-09-20 deploy — 'HTTP 403'), while the exact same request (bot UA, same headers) returns 200 consistently from this Mac — same Cloudflare-vs-Oregon-IP pattern as katedra.co.il. Fetched by the Mac relay instead.",
  "relay": "mac"
